From 5b34ae0f400893684bad97d09fe5ac54292986c9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Ersin=20KO=C3=87?= <ersinkoc@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 21:58:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat(desktop): an OS notification when approvals wait
 while the window is out of sight (draft)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

ADR-0048 decision 5, without a bridge to the hub's page (decision 2) and without a credential in the shell: the
web app already writes the waiting-approval count into the page title (`(N) …`); the shell watches title changes
(Tauri `on_document_title_changed`) and, when N grows while the window is hidden, minimized or not focused, shows
one OS notification with the count only. Words from locales/{en,tr}/notify.ftl through agora-i18n; the shell's
own screen reports the system language (`use_locale`). The main window is now built in `setup` from its
tauri.conf.json entry (`create: false`) so the title watch can be attached.

Draft: tauri-plugin-notification pulls zbus (Linux D-Bus) whose zvariant/zbus_names carry 2026 "unmaintained"
advisories, so cargo-deny for the desktop workspace fails; the choice is in the PR.

Signed-off-by: Ersin KOÇ <ersinkoc@gmail.com>
